  "details": "This is a bit of a mouthful!\n\nIn the VRChat client, when content gating is on, users wearing an avatar that contains an affecting content gate will display a lock in place of the profile picture. This is intended behavior.\n\nHowever, if you go on the VRChat website, and look up the name of the user still wearing a content gated avatar, the profile picture shows up, as if there is no content gate in place; does not display a profile picture lock.",
